neoxify-patch header: ios-dns-close

Closes a DoH connection whose TLS handshake failed, in the iOS engine. app/dns
returned the error and dropped the connection, which is a link dispatched
through the proxy, so each one stayed until the outbound gave up on it --
one per lookup while the DoH server cannot be reached (after a network
switch, or where it is blocked), which is exactly when lookups fall back to
TCP and open more. Written against xray-core v26.6.27 (45cf2898ab12),
app/dns/nameserver_doh.go. Applied by apps/mobile/scripts/xray-core-patch.sh,
for the iOS build only. Guarded by TestEngineMemoryBudget (plugins/vpn/xray),
2026-11-17.

--- a/app/dns/nameserver_doh.go
+++ b/app/dns/nameserver_doh.go
@@ -101,6 +101,11 @@
 				if !h2c {
 					conn = utls.UClient(conn, &utls.Config{ServerName: url.Hostname()}, utls.HelloChrome_Auto)
 					if err := conn.(*utls.UConn).HandshakeContext(ctx); err != nil {
+						// neoxify-patch: ios-dns-close. Closed, not dropped: the
+						// connection under it is a dispatched link through the
+						// proxy, which otherwise stays until its idle timeout --
+						// one per lookup while DoH cannot be reached.
+						conn.Close()
 						return nil, err
 					}
 				}
